(
  'lip-tints-guide-pakistan',
  $$Lip Tints in Pakistan: The Complete Guide to Long-Lasting Colour (2026)$$,
  $$What lip tints are, how to apply them so they last, and the best lip and cheek tints to buy in Pakistan — from glossy jelly tints to long-wear stains.$$,
  'Makeup', 'June 24, 2026', '7 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/lip-tints-guide-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>Lip tints are the easiest way to wear colour: lighter than lipstick, longer-lasting than gloss, and so forgiving you can swipe them on without a mirror. They've become the most-loved lip product among K-beauty fans in Pakistan — and for our climate, a long-wear tint makes far more sense than a heavy lipstick that melts by noon. Here's everything you need to know.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What is a lip tint?</h2>
<p>A lip tint stains the lips with a wash of buildable colour instead of sitting on top like traditional lipstick. The result is a "your lips but better" finish that looks natural, feels weightless, and fades evenly rather than patchily. Tints come in a few textures, each with a different feel.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Types of lip tint</h2>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Finish &amp; best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Water / jelly tint</td><td>Fresh, glossy, sheer — the classic dewy K-beauty look</td></tr><tr><td>Gel / peptide tint</td><td>Hydrating with a soft sheen; comfortable for dry lips</td></tr><tr><td>Matte / long-wear stain</td><td>Maximum staying power for all-day or events</td></tr><tr><td>Lip-and-cheek tint</td><td>Multi-use — colour for lips and a flush for cheeks</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Why lip tints suit Pakistan's climate</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Heat-proof colour.</strong> A stain grips the lips, so it survives chai, food and humidity far better than creamy lipstick.</li>
<li><strong>Lightweight feel.</strong> No heavy, drying layer in already-warm weather.</li>
<li><strong>Effortless for everyday.</strong> One swipe gives a polished look for work, university or running errands.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to apply lip tint so it lasts</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Start on clean, dry lips.</strong> Tints grip best without balm underneath (apply balm first only if your lips are very dry).</li>
<li><strong>Build from the centre out.</strong> Dab colour in the middle and blend outward with a fingertip for a natural gradient.</li>
<li><strong>Layer for intensity.</strong> Two thin layers last longer and look better than one thick one.</li>
<li><strong>For all-day wear,</strong> blot, add a second layer, and let it set for a minute before eating or drinking.</li>
<li><strong>Define the edges</strong> with a <a href="/blog/lip-liner-guide-pakistan">lip liner</a> if you want a crisper shape.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Choosing your shade</h2>
<p>Most Pakistani skin tones look beautiful in warm berries, roses, corals and brick-reds. For everyday, a my-lips-but-better rose or coral is foolproof; for events, a deeper berry or red tint reads bold without the weight of full lipstick. When in doubt, a multi-use lip-and-cheek tint in a rosy shade flatters almost everyone.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Lip tints to buy in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, imported and available with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Hydrating peptide tints:</strong> the viral <a href="/product/rhode-peptide-lip-tints">Rhode Peptide Lip Tints</a> and <a href="/product/rhode-lip-tint-raspberry-jelly">Rhode Lip Tint in Raspberry Jelly</a> — glossy, nourishing and buildable.</li>
<li><strong>Fresh jelly finish:</strong> the <a href="/product/milk-jelly-tints">Milk Jelly Tints</a> for a sheer, dewy wash of colour.</li>
<li><strong>Glossy everyday:</strong> the <a href="/product/pixi-lipglow">Pixi LipGlow</a> or the <a href="/product/kiko-milano-lip-gloss">Kiko Milano 3D Hydra Lip Gloss</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Long-wear colour:</strong> the <a href="/product/huda-beauty-icon-liquid-lipstick">Huda Beauty Icon Liquid Lipstick</a> for events.</li>
<li><strong>Lip-and-cheek multitasker:</strong> the <a href="/product/glow-recipe-watermelon-flush">Glow Recipe Watermelon Flush</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse all <a href="/shop?category=Lip+%26+Cheek+Tints">lip &amp; cheek tints</a> or the full <a href="/shop?taxon=makeup">makeup edit</a>.</p><a class="blog-cta" href="/shop?category=Lip+%26+Cheek+Tints">Shop Lip &amp; Cheek Tints →</a>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What is the difference between a lip tint and a lipstick?</h3>
<p>A tint stains the lips with lightweight, buildable colour that fades evenly; lipstick sits on top with fuller, heavier colour. Tints feel lighter and last longer through food and heat.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I make a lip tint last longer?</h3>
<p>Apply to clean, dry lips, build two thin layers, and blot between them. A lip liner underneath also helps it grip and hold its shape.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Are lip tints good for dry lips?</h3>
<p>Choose a hydrating gel or peptide tint, and apply a thin balm first if your lips are very dry. Matte long-wear stains can feel drier, so save those for events.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Which lip tint shade suits Pakistani skin?</h3>
<p>Warm berries, roses, corals and brick-reds flatter most Pakistani skin tones. A rosy lip-and-cheek tint is the most foolproof everyday choice.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Lightweight, long-lasting and effortless, lip tints are the smartest lip product for Pakistan's climate. Start with a hydrating everyday rose or coral and build from there. Explore the full range in our <a href="/shop?category=Lip+%26+Cheek+Tints">lip &amp; cheek tints</a> edit — authentic, with cash on delivery across Pakistan.</p>$html$
),
(
  'how-to-contour-pakistan',
  $$How to Contour Your Face: A Simple Step-by-Step Guide (2026)$$,
  $$Where to place contour, how to blend it, and how to choose the right shade for warm Pakistani skin tones — plus the products to do it with.$$,
  'Makeup', 'June 24, 2026', '7 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/how-to-contour-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>Contouring sounds intimidating, but it's really just shadow: placing a slightly deeper shade where the face naturally recedes, to add definition. Done lightly, it sculpts and slims; done heavily, it looks muddy. This simple guide shows you exactly where to put contour, how to blend it, and which shade suits warm Pakistani skin.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The golden rule of contouring</h2>
<p>Contour goes where you want shadow (to push areas back), and highlight goes where light hits (to bring areas forward). Together they sculpt the face. The two non-negotiables: <strong>choose the right shade</strong>, and <strong>blend until there are no harsh lines</strong>.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Where to apply contour</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Hollows of the cheeks</strong> — suck in your cheeks to find the natural dip; this is the classic sculpting spot.</li>
<li><strong>Temples and along the hairline</strong> — to frame the forehead.</li>
<li><strong>Along the jawline</strong> — to define and slim.</li>
<li><strong>Sides of the nose</strong> — a tiny amount to slim, blended well.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Cream or powder?</h2>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cream contour</td><td>Dry/normal skin and a natural, skin-like finish; apply before powder</td></tr><tr><td>Powder / bronzer</td><td>Oily skin and easy blending; apply after foundation and powder</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<p>For most people in Pakistan's humidity, a <strong>powder bronzer</strong> used lightly as contour is the easiest, longest-lasting option.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Choosing your shade</h2>
<p>The most common mistake is a contour that's too grey or too dark. For warm Pakistani skin tones, choose a shade only <strong>one to two levels deeper than your skin, with a warm or neutral (not ashy-grey) undertone</strong>. A warm bronze reads as a natural shadow; a cool grey reads as dirt. Build slowly — you can always add more.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to contour, step by step</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Start with your base</strong> — <a href="/blog/best-foundation-in-pakistan">foundation</a> and concealer first.</li>
<li><strong>Apply contour</strong> to the hollows of the cheeks, temples and jaw using a small amount.</li>
<li><strong>Blend upward and back</strong> with a brush or sponge until there's no visible line — this is 80% of the result.</li>
<li><strong>Add blush</strong> to the apples of the cheeks (see our <a href="/blog/how-to-apply-blush-pakistan">blush guide</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Finish with highlighter</strong> on the high points (see our <a href="/blog/how-to-apply-highlighter-pakistan">highlighter guide</a>) and set with a setting spray.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Products to contour with in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, imported and available with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Easy bronzer-contour:</strong> the <a href="/product/pixi-bronzer">Pixi On-the-Glow Bronze</a>, or the all-in-one <a href="/product/pixi-blush-bronzer-duo">Pixi Blush + Bronzer Duo</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Brighten the high points:</strong> the <a href="/product/tarte-shape-tape-creamy-concealer">Tarte Shape Tape Concealer</a> under the eyes and on the centre of the face.</li>
<li><strong>The right tools:</strong> a tapered brush from the <a href="/product/real-techniques-brush-set">Real Techniques Everyday Essentials Set</a> makes blending effortless.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse all <a href="/shop?category=Face+Makeup">face makeup</a> or the full <a href="/shop?taxon=makeup">makeup edit</a>.</p><a class="blog-cta" href="/shop?category=Face+Makeup">Shop Face Makeup →</a>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Where do you apply contour?</h3>
<p>In the hollows of the cheeks, along the temples and hairline, along the jawline, and lightly down the sides of the nose — anywhere you want to create natural shadow.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What shade should I use to contour?</h3>
<p>One to two shades deeper than your skin, with a warm or neutral undertone. Avoid ashy-grey shades, which look like dirt on warm Pakistani skin.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Do you contour before or after foundation?</h3>
<p>Cream contour goes after foundation but before powder; powder contour and bronzer go after you've set your base.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Is bronzer the same as contour?</h3>
<p>Not quite — contour adds shadow (cooler/neutral, in the hollows), while bronzer adds warmth (where the sun hits). Many people use a warm bronzer lightly as an easy everyday contour.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Right shade, light hand, endless blending — that's contouring. Start with a warm powder bronzer in the cheek hollows and build slowly. Find your tools in our <a href="/shop?category=Face+Makeup">face makeup</a> edit, authentic and with cash on delivery across Pakistan.</p>$html$
),
(
  'eye-makeup-for-beginners-pakistan',
  $$Eye Makeup for Beginners: A Simple Step-by-Step Guide (2026)$$,
  $$A beginner-friendly guide to everyday eye makeup — eyeshadow, eyeliner, kajal and mascara — with simple steps and the products to start with in Pakistan.$$,
  'Makeup', 'June 24, 2026', '8 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/eye-makeup-for-beginners-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>Eye makeup is where most beginners feel lost — too many brushes, too many shades, too many tutorials that assume you already know what you're doing. This guide strips it back to a simple, wearable everyday eye look you can actually recreate, then shows you how to build from there.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The four pieces of eye makeup</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Eyeshadow</strong> — adds depth and colour to the lids.</li>
<li><strong>Eyeliner / kajal</strong> — defines the lash line and shapes the eye.</li>
<li><strong>Mascara</strong> — lifts and separates the lashes; the one step that instantly opens the eyes.</li>
<li><strong>Brows</strong> (optional) — frame everything.</li>
</ul>
<p>You don't need all of them at once. If you do just one thing, do mascara.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">A simple everyday eye, step by step</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Prime the lid</strong> with a little concealer or base so colour grips and doesn't crease.</li>
<li><strong>Sweep a neutral shade</strong> (soft brown or warm beige) across the whole lid.</li>
<li><strong>Deepen the outer corner</strong> with a slightly darker brown and blend into the crease — this is what adds dimension.</li>
<li><strong>Line the upper lash line</strong> with kajal or a fine liner, staying close to the lashes. Keep it thin for daytime.</li>
<li><strong>Finish with mascara</strong>, wiggling the wand from root to tip.</li>
</ul>
<p>For warm Pakistani skin tones, <strong>browns, bronzes, golds and warm taupes</strong> are the most flattering and forgiving everyday shades.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Kajal — the Pakistani staple</h2>
<p>Kajal is the heart of South Asian eye makeup, and a smudge of it along the waterline or lash line transforms a face in seconds. The trick is making it <em>last</em> in heat and humidity without smudging down — we cover exactly how in our <a href="/blog/how-to-apply-kajal-make-it-last-pakistan">guide to applying kajal so it lasts all day</a>.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Beginner tips that make a big difference</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Build slowly.</strong> Tap excess shadow off the brush first; you can always add more.</li>
<li><strong>Blend, blend, blend.</strong> Soft edges look professional; hard lines look unfinished.</li>
<li><strong>Less is more for day.</strong> A neutral lid + liner + mascara is a complete look.</li>
<li><strong>Set the under-eye</strong> with a little powder to stop mascara and liner transferring in the heat.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Eye makeup to start with in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>A versatile palette:</strong> the <a href="/product/christine-velvet-eyeshadow-palette-28-colors">Christine Velvet Eyeshadow Palette (28 colours)</a> covers neutral everyday looks and bold evening ones.</li>
<li><strong>Lashes:</strong> the <a href="/product/mascara">Rivaj UK Volume Strength Mascara</a> lifts and adds volume.</li>
<li><strong>The right brushes:</strong> the <a href="/product/real-techniques-brush-set">Real Techniques Everyday Essentials Set</a> includes the blending brushes that make eyeshadow easy.</li>
<li><strong>Base &amp; setting:</strong> use a touch of <a href="/product/tarte-shape-tape-creamy-concealer">Tarte Shape Tape Concealer</a> as a lid primer.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse all <a href="/shop?category=Eyes">eye makeup</a> or the full <a href="/shop?taxon=makeup">makeup edit</a>. Building a full face? See our <a href="/blog/best-foundation-in-pakistan">foundation guide</a>.</p><a class="blog-cta" href="/shop?category=Eyes">Shop Eye Makeup →</a>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What eye makeup should a beginner start with?</h3>
<p>Start with mascara and a single neutral eyeshadow, then add a thin line of kajal or liner. That's a complete, wearable everyday look.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What eyeshadow colours suit Pakistani skin?</h3>
<p>Warm browns, bronzes, golds and taupes are the most flattering and forgiving for warm/medium Pakistani skin tones.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I stop eye makeup smudging in the heat?</h3>
<p>Prime the lid, set the under-eye with a little powder, and choose long-wear/waterproof kajal and mascara. Our kajal guide covers this in detail.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">In what order does eye makeup go on?</h3>
<p>Primer/base, then eyeshadow, then liner/kajal, then mascara last. Do your eyes before foundation if you're prone to shadow fallout.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Keep it simple: a neutral lid, a thin line of kajal and a coat of mascara is a polished everyday eye anyone can do. Build confidence there, then experiment. Find your starting kit in our <a href="/shop?category=Eyes">eye makeup</a> edit, authentic and with cash on delivery across Pakistan.</p>$html$
),
(
  'how-to-apply-blush-pakistan',
  $$How to Apply Blush: Cream, Liquid & Powder (2026 Guide)$$,
  $$Where to put blush for your face shape, how to choose cream vs liquid vs powder, and the best blushes for a natural flush in Pakistan.$$,
  'Makeup', 'June 24, 2026', '7 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/how-to-apply-blush-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>Blush is the fastest way to look healthy, awake and alive — it's the step that makes the difference between "wearing makeup" and looking radiant. Yet it's easy to get wrong: too much, too low, or the wrong formula that slides off in the heat. Here's how to apply blush for a natural, lasting flush.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Where to apply blush</h2>
<p>The safest, most flattering placement for almost everyone: smile, and apply blush to the <strong>apples of the cheeks</strong>, then blend up and back toward the temple. Keeping colour higher on the cheek (rather than low and round) lifts the face. A tiny touch on the bridge of the nose ties the look together for a sun-kissed effect.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Cream, liquid or powder?</h2>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Formula</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Liquid blush</td><td>A natural, dewy, lasting flush; a little goes a long way</td></tr><tr><td>Cream / stick blush</td><td>Dry/normal skin and a fresh, skin-like glow; blends with fingers</td></tr><tr><td>Powder blush</td><td>Oily skin and easy control; longest-lasting in humidity</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<p>In Pakistan's heat, <strong>liquid and cream blushes</strong> give the most natural, lasting result on most skin — but if you're very oily, a powder blush set over your base will hold best.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Choosing your shade</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Fair to light:</strong> soft pinks and peaches.</li>
<li><strong>Medium to tan:</strong> warm corals, rosy pinks and terracotta — the most flattering range for most Pakistani skin.</li>
<li><strong>Deep:</strong> rich berries, brick and deep coral, which glow rather than disappear.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to apply blush, step by step</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Apply after foundation.</strong> Cream and liquid blush go on right after foundation (before powder); powder blush goes on last.</li>
<li><strong>Start with very little.</strong> Dab liquid/cream on the apples with a finger, or tap a powder brush off first — you can always build.</li>
<li><strong>Blend up and out</strong> toward the temple so there's no harsh edge.</li>
<li><strong>Layer to build,</strong> rather than applying a lot at once.</li>
<li><strong>Pair with <a href="/blog/how-to-apply-highlighter-pakistan">highlighter</a></strong> on the cheekbones for extra glow, and set with a setting spray.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Blushes to buy in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, imported and available with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Natural liquid flush:</strong> the cult <a href="/product/rare-beauty-liquid-blush-hope">Rare Beauty Liquid Blush</a> or the <a href="/product/nars-afterglow-liquid-blush">NARS Afterglow Liquid Blush</a> — highly pigmented, so use a tiny amount.</li>
<li><strong>Affordable liquid options:</strong> the <a href="/product/sheglam-liquid-blush-all-shades">SHEGLAM Liquid Blush</a> or <a href="/product/makeup-revolution-super-dewy-liquid-blush">Makeup Revolution Super Dewy Liquid Blush</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Easy cream sticks:</strong> the <a href="/product/pixi-blush-sticks-ruby-juicy-fleur">Pixi On-the-Glow Blush Sticks</a> blend with fingertips in seconds.</li>
<li><strong>A luxe classic:</strong> the <a href="/product/dior-blush-rosy-glow">Dior Blush Rosy Glow</a>.</li>
<li><strong>The right tool:</strong> a <a href="/product/blush-brush-by-real-techniques">Real Techniques Blush Brush</a> for powder.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse all <a href="/shop?category=Lip+%26+Cheek+Tints">blushes &amp; tints</a> or the full <a href="/shop?taxon=makeup">makeup edit</a>.</p><a class="blog-cta" href="/product/rare-beauty-liquid-blush-hope">Shop the Rare Beauty Liquid Blush →</a>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Where exactly do you put blush?</h3>
<p>On the apples of the cheeks (smile to find them), blended up toward the temple. Keeping it higher lifts the face.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Is cream or powder blush better?</h3>
<p>Cream and liquid give a natural, dewy, lasting flush and suit most skin; powder is easiest to control and lasts best on very oily skin in humidity.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Do you apply blush before or after foundation?</h3>
<p>Cream and liquid blush go on after foundation but before powder; powder blush goes on after your base is set.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I stop blush looking too heavy?</h3>
<p>Start with a tiny amount and build. With pigmented liquid blushes, a single dot per cheek is often enough — blend quickly before it sets.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Blush on the apples, blended up and out, in a warm shade for your tone — it's the quickest way to look radiant. Liquid and cream formulas win for a natural flush in our climate. Find yours in the <a href="/shop?category=Lip+%26+Cheek+Tints">blush &amp; tint</a> edit, authentic and with cash on delivery across Pakistan.</p>$html$
),
(
  'lip-liner-guide-pakistan',
  $$How to Use Lip Liner for Fuller, Longer-Lasting Lips (2026)$$,
  $$What lip liner is for, how to use it to define and subtly plump your lips, and how to make lip colour last all day — plus the products to use in Pakistan.$$,
  'Makeup', 'June 24, 2026', '6 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/lip-liner-guide-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>Lip liner is one of the most underrated products in any makeup bag. It defines the lips, stops colour bleeding, makes lipstick and tint last dramatically longer, and can even make lips look subtly fuller — all from one inexpensive pencil. Here's how to use it properly.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What lip liner does</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Defines the shape</strong> of your lips for a crisp, polished edge.</li>
<li><strong>Stops feathering</strong> — colour bleeding into the fine lines around the lips.</li>
<li><strong>Makes colour last</strong> — lining and lightly filling the lips gives lipstick or tint a base to grip.</li>
<li><strong>Subtly plumps</strong> — lining just outside your natural line (a hair's width) creates the look of fuller lips.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to use lip liner, step by step</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Start in the centre</strong> of the upper lip and follow your natural line out to each corner, then do the lower lip.</li>
<li><strong>Use small, light strokes</strong> rather than one heavy line — more control, more natural.</li>
<li><strong>For longer wear, lightly fill in</strong> the whole lip with the liner before applying your lipstick or tint.</li>
<li><strong>To plump,</strong> trace a hair's width <em>outside</em> your natural line at the centre of the lips — overdo it and it looks obvious, so keep it subtle.</li>
<li><strong>Blend the inner edge</strong> so there's no visible ring once your lip colour fades.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Choosing your shade</h2>
<p>Two approaches both work: a <strong>nude/your-natural-lip shade</strong> that goes with everything, or a liner that <strong>matches your lipstick or tint</strong>. Avoid a liner much darker than your lip colour — the harsh outlined look is dated. For most Pakistani skin tones, a warm rosy-nude or soft berry is the most versatile everyday choice.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Make your lip colour last all day</h2>
<p>The combination that survives chai, lunch and heat: line the lips, lightly fill them with liner, apply your <a href="/blog/lip-tints-guide-pakistan">lip tint</a> or lipstick, blot with a tissue, then add one more thin layer. The liner base grips the colour so it fades evenly instead of disappearing from the centre.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Lip liner &amp; lip products to buy in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>An everyday liner:</strong> the long-wearing <a href="/product/lip-liner">Rivaj UK Waterproof Lip Pencil</a> defines and holds colour in place.</li>
