<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What is lip liner used for?</h3>
<p>To define the lip shape, stop colour bleeding, make lipstick and tint last longer, and subtly create the look of fuller lips.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Should lip liner be darker than your lipstick?</h3>
<p>No — match it to your lipstick or your natural lip colour. A liner much darker than the lip looks dated and harsh.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I make my lipstick last all day?</h3>
<p>Line and lightly fill the lips with liner first, apply colour, blot, then add a second thin layer. The liner gives the colour a base to grip.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Can lip liner make my lips look bigger?</h3>
<p>Yes, subtly — trace just outside your natural line at the centre of the lips and blend. Keep it within a hair's width so it looks natural.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
